KNOWNBUG: N5008 [temp.inst]/4 -- unordered_set::insert comes from the
std::__detail::_Insert CRTP mixin; its odr-used member body is never
instantiated ("no body for callee ..._Insert<...>::insert"), so insert
is a no-op and count() is wrong.  Found dog-fooding
src/util/find_symbols.cpp.  Flip to CORE when fixed.

UPDATE 2026-07-17: three front-end defects in the chain are FIXED and
the whole insert path now CONVERTS (no missing bodies, no incomplete
warnings): (1) the deferred-member drain in instantiate_template used
an unbounded rfind("::") to strip the "tag-" marker, landing inside
template ARGUMENTS for _Insert<..., _Hashtable_traits<0,1,1>, 1> and
missing every deferred member (cpp11_unordered_set_insert's original
"no body"); (2) derived-to-PRIVATE-base conversion in a FRIEND of the
derived class was rejected ([class.access.base]/4-5; test
cpp98_friend_private_base_conversion) -- _AllocNode(_Hashtable&
-> _Hashtable_alloc&) failed and _Insert::insert's body was dropped;
(3) an if-condition declaration's name leaked into the enclosing block
([stmt.pre]/6; test cpp98_condition_decl_scope) -- _M_insert_unique's
`__node` redeclaration failed conversion.  RESIDUAL: with everything
converting, the bucket-chain walk in _M_find_before_node does not
terminate within --unwind 30 (unwinding assertion fires; garbage node
pointers in the trace), so count() still returns wrong values --
suspect one more defect in the insert-side bucket linking
(_M_insert_unique_node / _M_insert_bucket_begin) or in the
single-bucket small-table mode.  Needs isolation.
